#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_education_management
msgid ""
".. image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/licence-AGPL--3-blue.svg\n"
"   :alt: License: AGPL-3\n"
"\n"
"Education management\n"
"====================\n"
"\n"
"Education addon according to Binovo standards:\n"
"\n"
"Groups:\n"
"\n"
"* User: a user can read all education data, but it can only write on exam records and attendances.\n"
"* Responsible: a responsible can do all operations on all models.\n"
"\n"
"Models:\n"
"\n"
"* Students and teachers: are partners with a boolean field that specifies if the partner is a student, a teacher or both of them. There also are some fields that characterize partners as students/teachers, some of those fields are only accessible for responsible.\n"
"* Courses: it is a model that defines general data of a group of courses, it is like a template of courses.\n"
"* Batches: this is the main model that defines data of a specific course, it has relations with: student, teachers, schedules, attendances and admission. Schedules and attendances are managed within the batch.\n"
"* Admission: an admission of a student on a batch.\n"
"\n"
"Flow:\n"
"\n"
"* Admission: it has 3 states: draft, done (Enrolled) and cancel. A draft admission is created and an action of Enroll admission can be launched to confirm the admission. If the student does not exists (it is match with e-mail or vat) it is created with admission data; if it exists students data are updated with the newest admission data. Students are also can be checked in a batch, they are listed. There also is a Cancel admission action to unlink these relation.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"Contributors\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"* Ugaitz Olaizola <uolaizola@binovo.es>\n"
"\n"
"Maintainer\n"
"----------\n"
"\n"
".. image:: /education_management/static/src/img/binovo.png\n"
"   :alt: Binovo IT Human Project SL\n"
"   :target: http://www.binovo.es\n"
"\n"
"This module is maintained by Binovo IT Human Project SL.\n"
msgstr ""

