#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_partner_remote_synchronization
msgid ""
".. image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/licence-AGPL--3-blue.svg\n"
"   :alt: License: AGPL-3\n"
"\n"
"Partner remote synchronization\n"
"==============================\n"
"\n"
"Partners synchronization to an Odoo external server:\n"
"\n"
"* Partners creation, write and delete action are synchronized to an external server via RPC calls.\n"
"\n"
"* Synchronizations are executed with delay via queue jobs.\n"
"\n"
"* Synchronization is simplified, and relational fields are not take into account, only if the relation is with another res.partner. Therefore \"many2many\", \"many2one\", \"one2many\" and \"reference\" are ignored.\n"
"\n"
"Tested Odoo versions: client v11.0 and remote server v16.0.\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"-------------\n"
"\n"
"Odoo client1\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"Check \"Do remote synchro\" boolean field in partners to activate synchronization of them.\n"
"\n"
"In the general settings per company, introduce external server data: server url, database name, user and password.\n"
"\n"
"Odoo server1\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"Create an API user with admin settings.\n"
"\n"
"Dependencies\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"Odoo client2\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"base_setup, queue_job, res_partner_external_id modules\n"
"\n"
"Odoo server2\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"res_partner_external_id\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"Contributors\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"* Ugaitz Olaizola <uolaizola@binovo.es>\n"
"* Imanol Aranburu <iaranburu@binovo.es>\n"
"\n"
"Maintainer\n"
"----------\n"
"\n"
".. image:: /partner_remote_synchronization/static/src/img/binovo_logo_peque.jpg\n"
"   :alt: Binovo IT Human Project SL\n"
"   :target: http://www.binovo.es\n"
"\n"
"This module is maintained by Binovo IT Human Project SL.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_hr_payroll_management
msgid ""
".. image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/licence-AGPL--3-blue.svg\n"
"   :alt: License: AGPL-3\n"
"\n"
"PayrollSecure: employee payroll management\n"
"==========================================\n"
"\n"
"PayrollSecure employee payroll secure distribution.\n"
"\n"
"Workflow:\n"
"\n"
"Launch Payroll import wizard from employees menu, upload a pdf containing all employees payrolls in a single file. Each page\n"
"must have the payroll information of a single employee. Validate an send payroll files.\n"
"\n"
"Models and fields:\n"
"\n"
"Employees: new payroll_encryption_key field to assign and encryption key to each employee to crypt payroll pdf files.\n"
"\n"
"Companies: PKCS12 file container with the certificate and password. Payroll management configuration data.\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"#. This addon does not depends on hr_employee_document, but install it to create an access button to the documents related to the employee that include payroll files. Each employee has access only for his payrolls.\n"
"#. Go to Technical menu, in System parameters create a new key \"base_setup.default_user_rights_minimal\" with Value to \"True\" inorder to create users associated to the employees with the minimal rights.\n"
"#. With a HR manager user, go to Employee configuration menu and in the company upload a PKCS12 file container with a certificate and password in order to sign payroll files.\n"
"\n"
"External dependencies\n"
"=====================\n"
"\n"
"This addon depends on pyhanko and sshpass.\n"
"\n"
